{"step_index":1014,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:15:56Z","input_tokens":2887,"cache_read_tokens":448438,"output_tokens":1966,"tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to add a 'Reset Response Lock' button in teacher.html and cross-device epoch-based unlock synchronization in index.html to clear 'You have already responded' locks both locally and remotely.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Teacher Reset Response Lock (\"You have already responded\")\n\n## 1. Overview & Problem Solved\nCurrently, [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) records a per-quiz completion lock (`ds_quiz_lock_<quizId>`) inside each student browser's `localStorage`, showing `\"You have already responded\"` (`#lock`) on reload. To let teachers unlock retakes across **all student devices remotely** (as well as their own local testing browser) without manually editing `#reset-quiz` URLs on every phone:\n\n1. Introduce a `lockEpoch` integer timestamp stored inside the remote `quizzes/{quizId}` record.\n2. Add a **`Reset Response Lock`** button in [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) right in the main action row (`#view-editor`), protected by `#confirm-modal`.\n3. Update [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) to save the active `lockEpoch` inside `localStorage` when taking/finishing the quiz, and automatically clear any stale `localStorage` lock when `remote.lockEpoch > local.epoch`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. File Modifications & Exact Technical Design\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) (Pre-Obfuscation Source -> Re-Hardened Dual Layer)\n- **UI Button:** Add `<button id=\"reset-lock-btn\" class=\"danger\" type=\"button\">Reset Response Lock</button>` in the `#view-editor` primary card action row alongside `Save to Quiz` and `Download Quiz File`.\n- **Shared Modal Dispatch (DRY):** Reuse `#confirm-modal` (`\"Are you sure this is what you want?\"` with `Yes`/`No`) via a `pendingAction` state (`'clearSub'` vs `'resetLock'`).\n- **Epoch Persistence (`currentLockEpoch`):**\n  - Initialize `let currentLockEpoch = 0;` and sync from `quiz.lockEpoch` inside `populateQuizData(quiz)`.\n  - Include `lockEpoch: currentLockEpoch` inside `buildQuizPayload()` so saving question edits **never** unlocks students mid-exam.\n- **Partial Remote Field Update (`EncryptedLocalDB.patchField`):**\n  - Add masked query parameter array `_vU` (`updateMask.fieldPaths=`).\n  - When **`Reset Response Lock`** -> **`Yes`** is confirmed:\n    - Set `nextEpoch = Date.now()`.\n    - Call `EncryptedLocalDB.patchField(quizId, 'lockEpoch', nextEpoch)` so only `lockEpoch` is updated without overwriting unsaved draft edits in the editor.\n    - Also call `localStorage.removeItem('ds_quiz_lock_' + quizId)` locally on the teacher's browser.\n    - Display `$('status-msg')`: `'Student response lock reset! Locked devices will unlock on reload.'`.\n- **Re-harden** via `harden.cjs` so the production [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) keeps two-layer AST obfuscation + RC4 stream cipher protection.\n\n### 2.2 [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) (Pre-Obfuscation Source -> Re-Hardened Dual Layer)\n- **Record Epoch on Start & Finish:**\n  - Save `epoch: Number(quizData && quizData.lockEpoch) || 0` in `localStorage.setItem(LOCK, ...)` inside both `$('go').onclick` (`state: 'started'`) and `finish()` (`state: 'done'`).\n- **Remote Unlock Verification Helper (`checkRemoteUnlock(data)`):**\n  - Called in `loadQuiz()` for both online `readQuiz()` and offline `#local-db-vault` fallback:\n    - If `LOCK` exists in `localStorage`, compare `remoteEpoch = Number(data && data.lockEpoch) || 0` against `localEpoch = Number(L && L.epoch) || 0`.\n    - If `remoteEpoch > localEpoch`: remove `LOCK` from `localStorage`, hide `#lock`, reveal `#start`, and initialize the quiz via `initDisplay(data)`.\n    - If `remoteEpoch <= localEpoch`: set `quizData = data` and call `showLock()` so `#lock` stays enforced (with `#lkdl` accurately reflecting `autoRecordQuiz`).\n- **Re-harden** via `harden.cjs` so the production [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) keeps two-layer AST obfuscation + RC4 stream cipher protection.\n\n### 2.3 Sync & Changelog\n- Re-sync updated hardened [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) to `quizzes/template`.\n- Append **Non-Major Patch 1.0.21** to [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md) per Rule 1.\n- Preserve `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` untouched (Rules 2 & 12) and maintain zero in-code comments (Rule 9).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency, Edge-Case, & Security Analysis\n\n| Scenario | Behavior | Protection |\n|---|---|---|\n| Existing student locked before feature existed (`L.epoch === undefined`) | `localEpoch` evaluates to `0` | First teacher reset sets `lockEpoch = Date.now() > 0`, automatically unlocking legacy locked browsers on reload. |\n| Teacher edits a question and clicks `Save to Quiz` | `buildQuizPayload()` sends preserved `currentLockEpoch` | `remoteEpoch === localEpoch`, so students remain locked. |\n| Student tries loading without teacher reset | `remoteEpoch <= localEpoch` | `#lock` renders immediately on startup with zero flash of `#start`, and remains locked after sync. |\n| Teacher accidentally taps `Reset Response Lock` | `#confirm-modal` intercepts before writing | Requires explicit **Yes** confirmation. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n1. **Hardened Source Audit:** Verify zero plaintext Firebase/Firestore/Google/`fetch`/helper strings and zero comments across compiled [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) and [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html).\n2. **End-to-End Epoch Unlock Test (Node VM + Live Firestore on `verify_probe_tmp`):**\n   - Seed `verify_probe_tmp` (`lockEpoch: 0`) -> simulate locked student `localStorage` (`{ state: 'done', epoch: 0 }`) -> run hardened `index.html` and assert `#lock` stays hidden/active (NOT unlocked).\n   - Run hardened `teacher.html` (`?quiz=verify_probe_tmp`), click **`reset-lock-btn`** -> click **`modal-yes-btn`**, verify Firestore `lockEpoch > 0` AND verify existing `title`/`questions` on `verify_probe_tmp` remained intact.\n   - Re-run hardened `index.html` with that same student `localStorage` (`epoch: 0`) -> verify `LOCK` is removed from `localStorage`, `#lock` gets `.hide`, `#start` has `.hide` removed, and `#go.disabled === false`.\n   - Re-lock student with `epoch = lockEpoch` -> reload without new reset -> verify `#lock` stays enforced!\n   - Clean up temporary `verify_probe_tmp` doc (`HTTP 200`).\n3. **Sync & Original File Check:** Verify `quizzes/template` updated (`HTTP 200`) and `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` unchanged.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
