{"step_index":1021,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:18:32Z","input_tokens":2970,"cache_read_tokens":455805,"output_tokens":2735,"thinking":"The user's clarification suggests creating a dedicated \"Reset\" tab to house the \"Reset Response Lock\" button, improving UI organization. This approach avoids cluttering the main \"Quiz Editor\" interface and offers a cleaner, more intuitive user experience. Placing the button in its own tab also signals a clear separation of function.\n\n\nCreated the \"Reset\" tab, distinct from the \"Quiz Editor\" and \"Submissions\" tabs, housing the \"Reset Response Lock\" button within a dedicated card to maintain UI clarity. Refactored the tab-switching logic to adhere to DRY principles, implementing a helper function to manage tab visibility, which simplifies the code and improves maintainability. The \"Reset\" tab includes a descriptive message for the button's function and a status area to update the UI on the outcomes of that action.\n\n\nThe tab-switching function is now refactored into a concise, reusable helper, minimizing code duplication and enhancing maintainability. This single function manages the active state and visibility of all three tabs uniformly. Furthermore, the confirmation modal is now reused for multiple actions, employing a `pendingAction` flag to distinguish between different confirmation scenarios, such as clearing submissions or resetting the lock, streamlining the user interaction flow.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Updated implementation plan to add a third 'Reset' tab in teacher.html housing the 'Reset Response Lock' button, confirmation modal reuse, and cross-device epoch unlock synchronization in index.html.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Add `Reset` Tab & Cross-Device Response Lock Reset\n\n## 1. Overview & Architecture\nOrganize reset controls cleanly into a new top-level **`Reset`** tab in [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) (`Quiz Editor` | `Submissions` | `Reset`) and implement remote cross-device epoch unlocking in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) so teachers can reset `\"You have already responded\"` across all student devices and their local test browser.\n\n---\n\n## 2. File Modifications & Exact Technical Design\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) (Pre-Obfuscation Source -> Re-Hardened Dual Layer)\n- **Top Navigation Bar (`.tab-nav`):**\n  - Add 3rd tab `<button id=\"tab-btn-reset\" class=\"tab-item\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>` beside `Quiz Editor` and `Submissions`.\n- **DRY Table-Driven Tab Switcher (`switchTab`):**\n  - Replace duplicated per-tab click handlers with a unified table-driven `switchTab(activeBtnId)` toggling `.active` and `.hide` across `['tab-btn-editor', 'view-editor']`, `['tab-btn-sub', 'view-sub']`, and `['tab-btn-reset', 'view-reset']`, calling `refreshSubmissions()` when switching to Submissions.\n- **`#view-reset` Card:**\n  - Add `<div id=\"view-reset\" class=\"hide\">` containing heading `Reset Response Lock`, description explaining unlocking `\"You have already responded\"` on reload, `<button id=\"reset-lock-btn\" class=\"danger\" type=\"button\">Reset Response Lock</button>`, and status indicator `<p id=\"reset-status-msg\">`.\n- **Shared Modal Dispatch (`#confirm-modal`):**\n  - Reuse `#confirm-modal` (`\"Are you sure this is what you want?\"` with `Yes`/`No`) via `pendingAction` (`'clearSub'` vs `'resetLock'`).\n- **Epoch Persistence (`currentLockEpoch`) & Partial Remote Patch:**\n  - Track `let currentLockEpoch = 0;` populated from `quiz.lockEpoch` in `populateQuizData()` and preserved inside `buildQuizPayload()` so ordinary `Save to Quiz` edits never unlock completed students mid-exam.\n  - Add masked `updateMask.fieldPaths=` array (`_vU`) and `EncryptedLocalDB.patchField(id, fieldName, val)`.\n  - On `Reset Response Lock` -> `Yes`:\n    - Set `nextEpoch = Date.now()`.\n    - Patch remote `lockEpoch` via `EncryptedLocalDB.patchField(quizId, 'lockEpoch', nextEpoch)` without overwriting unsaved editor drafts.\n    - Remove local `localStorage.removeItem('ds_quiz_lock_' + quizId)`.\n    - Set `#reset-status-msg` text to `'Student response lock reset! Locked devices will unlock on reload.'`.\n- **Re-harden** with Layer-1 AST obfuscation + Layer-2 RC4 stream cipher (`harden.cjs`).\n\n### 2.2 [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) (Pre-Obfuscation Source -> Re-Hardened Dual Layer)\n- **Store Epoch in Lock Record:**\n  - Persist `epoch: Number(quizData && quizData.lockEpoch) || 0` inside `localStorage` under `LOCK` in both `$('go').onclick` (`state: 'started'`) and `finish()` (`state: 'done'`).\n- **Cross-Device Unlock Check (`checkRemoteUnlock(data)`):**\n  - Invoked from `loadQuiz()` for both live remote `readQuiz(quizId)` and offline `#local-db-vault`:\n    - If `LOCK` exists, compare `remoteEpoch = Number(data && data.lockEpoch) || 0` against `localEpoch = Number(L && L.epoch) || 0`.\n    - When `remoteEpoch > localEpoch`: remove `LOCK`, hide `#lock`, reveal `#start`, and call `initDisplay(data)`.\n    - Otherwise: keep `quizData = data` and refresh `showLock()`.\n- **Re-harden** with Layer-1 AST obfuscation + Layer-2 RC4 stream cipher (`harden.cjs`).\n\n### 2.3 Sync & Changelog\n- Re-sync compiled [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) into Firestore `quizzes/template`.\n- Append **Non-Major Patch 1.0.21** to [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md) per Rule 1.\n- Preserve `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` completely untouched (Rules 2 & 12) and maintain zero comments (Rule 9).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency, Performance, & Edge-Case Analysis\n\n| Scenario / Component | Dependency | Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tab bar layout on narrow screens | `.tab-nav` (`flex: 1` per `.tab-item`) | Overflow with 3 tabs on small phones | Short 1-word label `Reset` fits cleanly alongside `Quiz Editor` and `Submissions`. |\n| Unsaved editor edits during Reset | `patchField` with `updateMask` | Overwriting unsaved draft questions | Partial `PATCH` updates ONLY `lockEpoch`, keeping active questions safe. |\n| Legacy locked devices (`L.epoch === undefined`) | `localEpoch` fallback `0` | Old locked browsers failing to unlock | Any reset sets `lockEpoch = Date.now() > 0`, unlocking legacy locks automatically. |\n| Mid-exam teacher edits (`Save to Quiz`) | `currentLockEpoch` in `buildQuizPayload()` | Accidental unlock on typo fix | `currentLockEpoch` is preserved across saves until `Reset Response Lock` is explicitly triggered. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n1. **Hardened Audit:** Verify zero Firebase/Firestore/Google/`fetch`/helper strings and zero comments in compiled [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) and [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html).\n2. **End-to-End Reset Tab & Epoch Unlock Test (Node VM + Live Firestore on `verify_probe_tmp`):**\n   - Run compiled `teacher.html` bootstrapper: click `#tab-btn-reset` -> verify `#view-reset` becomes visible and `#view-editor` / `#view-sub` hide; click `#reset-lock-btn` -> verify `#confirm-modal` opens; click `#modal-yes-btn` -> verify `#reset-status-msg` shows success and `verify_probe_tmp` in Firestore receives `lockEpoch > 0` without altering `title`/`questions`.\n   - Run compiled `index.html` bootstrapper with a stale locked `localStorage` (`epoch: 0`) against `verify_probe_tmp`: verify `LOCK` is cleared from `localStorage`, `#lock` hides, `#start` unhides, and `#go.disabled === false`.\n   - Re-seed student `localStorage` with `epoch = lockEpoch` and reload without a new reset: verify `#lock` stays active and locked!\n   - Clean up temporary `verify_probe_tmp` doc (`HTTP 200`).\n3. **Sync & Original File Check:** Confirm `quizzes/template` updated (`HTTP 200`) and `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` unchanged.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
